{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.SelectionRuleQuantumIntegerForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.SelectionRuleQuantumIntegerForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.tau_anchors_assemble_quantum_integer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.tau_anchors_assemble_quantum_integer","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelectionRuleQuantumIntegerForm.lean#L62-L73","doc":"**The categorical `[2]_q` derivation, assembled.** Substituting `b = [2]_q = q + q⁻¹` into the\nanchor assembly gives `τ` directly in the quantum integer:\n`(1 + lw(3))/lw(2) = 3(3[2]² + 2)/(4([2] + 2))`. This is the `lw → τ` half of the keystone,\nentirely a function of the Hecke eigenvalue gap `[2]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.tau_from_quantum_integer_anchors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.tau_from_quantum_integer_anchors","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelectionRuleQuantumIntegerForm.lean#L53-L60","doc":"**The τ assembly from the three `[2]_q` anchors.** With the mean quantum dimensions\n`lw(1) = 1`, `lw(2) = (b + 2)/3`, `lw(3) = (3b² − 2)/4` (here `b = [2]_q`), the kernel trace\n`τ = (lw(1) + lw(3))/lw(2)` equals `3(3b² + 2)/(4(b + 2))` — `TauQuantumIntegerForm`'s closed form.\nStated for a generic `b` with `b + 2 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.selection_rule_c3_quantum_integer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.selection_rule_c3_quantum_integer","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelectionRuleQuantumIntegerForm.lean#L43-L51","doc":"**`lw(3)` (the Family-A / proton anchor) in bar-even `[2]_q` form:**\n`(3q² + 4 + 3q⁻²)/4 = (3[2]_q² − 2)/4` with `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. The corpus's `h`-form uses the\nbar-odd `h = q − q⁻¹` via `(q−q⁻¹)² = [2]_q² − 4`; this is the bar-even quantum-integer form that\nmatches `TauQuantumIntegerForm`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}